# Database objects — `insight` schema

All SqlMonitor / SmartMonitor persistence objects (tables, views, procedures, functions) that the app owns must be created in the **`insight`** schema — never `dbo` (except temporary/demo scripts that explicitly say otherwise).

## Schema

```sql
IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.schemas WHERE name = N'insight')
    EXEC(N'CREATE SCHEMA insight');
```

## Naming

| Object | Pattern | Example |
|--------|---------|---------|
| Tables | `insight.<snake_or_domain_name>` | `insight.metric_samples`, `insight.IdxCat_Table` |
| Procedures | `insight.USP_Insight_<Area>_<Action>` | `insight.USP_Insight_IndexCatalog_Refresh` |
| Constraints / indexes | Prefer `PK_insight_…`, `IX_insight_…`, `DF_insight_…` | |

## Rules

1. New SQL under `scripts/sql/`, `phase2/queries/`, or provider helpers must target **`insight.*`**.
2. Procedure names start with **`USP_Insight_`** (schema still `insight`).
3. App code that probes catalog objects must look for `schema = insight` (not `dbo`).
4. Grants for the app login must be on `insight.<object>`.
5. Soft-fail if objects are missing — do not require catalog for core UI.

